    "shortDesc": "Unilateral primary osteoarthritis, right knee",
    "longDesc": "Unilateral primary osteoarthritis, right knee",
    "plainEnglish": "This code describes wear-and-tear arthritis that specifically affects only the right knee, where the cartilage that cushions the joint has gradually worn down over time. This is the most common type of arthritis and typically develops slowly from years of use, aging, or sometimes from past injuries. People with this condition usually experience pain, stiffness, swelling, and difficulty walking or bending the right knee, especially after activity or in the morning.",
    "whoUses": "Orthopedic surgeons, rheumatologists, primary care physicians, and physical therapists commonly use this code when treating knee arthritis. It frequently appears on patient EOB statements as it's a common chronic condition that leads to multiple office visits, imaging, medications, injections, or eventual knee replacement surgery.",
