    "shortDesc": "Primary osteoarthritis, right shoulder",
    "longDesc": "Primary osteoarthritis, right shoulder",
    "plainEnglish": "Primary osteoarthritis of the right shoulder is a degenerative condition where the protective cartilage in your shoulder joint gradually breaks down over time, causing the bones to rub together. This wear-and-tear happens without an underlying injury or disease and typically develops as people age, leading to pain, stiffness, reduced mobility, and sometimes a grinding sensation in the shoulder. The condition can make everyday activities like reaching, lifting, or throwing increasingly difficult.",
    "whoUses": "Orthopedic surgeons, rheumatologists, and physical medicine & rehabilitation specialists commonly diagnose and treat primary shoulder osteoarthritis. This code frequently appears on patient EOB statements, especially for those seeking joint injections, physical therapy, imaging studies, or surgical intervention.",
