    "shortDesc": "Spondylosis w/o myelopathy or radiculopathy, lumbar region",
    "longDesc": "Spondylosis without myelopathy or radiculopathy, lumbar region",
    "plainEnglish": "Spondylosis is wear-and-tear arthritis of the spine, where the discs between vertebrae deteriorate and bone spurs develop over time. In the lumbar (lower back) region, this condition causes the spine to become stiff and may limit your movement, but it isn't currently causing nerve damage or radiating pain down your legs. You might experience localized lower back pain or stiffness, especially with certain movements.",
    "whoUses": "Primary care physicians, orthopedic surgeons, neurologists, and physiatrists (physical medicine specialists) commonly use this code when evaluating chronic lower back pain and degenerative disc disease. It frequently appears on patient EOB statements as it's a common age-related condition found during imaging for back pain complaints.",
