    "plainEnglish": "Cervicalgia is neck pain that occurs in the cervical region—the upper part of your spine where your neck bones are located. This pain can range from mild stiffness to sharp discomfort and may result from muscle strain, poor posture, injury, or age-related wear and tear on the spine. You might feel soreness when moving your head, tightness in the neck muscles, or pain that radiates down into your shoulders.",
