    "rawCode": "M5451",
    "shortDesc": "Vertebrogenic low back pain",
    "longDesc": "Vertebrogenic low back pain",
    "plainEnglish": "Vertebrogenic low back pain means your lower back pain is caused directly by a problem with one or more of your vertebrae (the bones that make up your spine) or the joints between them. This can result from wear and tear, misalignment, disc issues, or other structural problems in the spine itself. You typically feel pain in the lower back area, which may worsen with certain movements or positions.",
    "whoUses": "Primary care doctors, orthopedic specialists, spine surgeons, physical medicine and rehabilitation physicians, and chiropractors commonly use this code when diagnosing patients with spine-related lower back pain confirmed by imaging or clinical findings. It frequently appears on patient EOB statements as it is a common diagnosis for insured patients seeking treatment for chronic or acute back problems.",
