    "code": "M79.3",
    "rawCode": "M793",
    "shortDesc": "Panniculitis, unspecified",
    "longDesc": "Panniculitis, unspecified",
    "plainEnglish": "Panniculitis is inflammation of the fatty tissue layer beneath your skin, which causes painful lumps, redness, and swelling in affected areas. This condition can occur anywhere on the body where there's a layer of fat under the skin, and while it's often triggered by infections, autoimmune disorders, or trauma, sometimes doctors can't pinpoint the exact cause—which is why it's labeled 'unspecified.' The inflamed fatty tissue feels tender, warm, and may form nodules that are uncomfortable to touch.",
    "whoUses": "Primary care physicians, dermatologists, and rheumatologists commonly diagnose and treat panniculitis. This code appears on EOB statements when patients present with unexplained fatty tissue inflammation and after other specific causes have been ruled out, making it a frequent diagnosis in dermatology and rheumatology practices.",
