    "code": "M79.622",
    "rawCode": "M79622",
    "shortDesc": "Pain in left upper arm",
    "longDesc": "Pain in left upper arm",
    "plainEnglish": "This code describes pain located in the left upper arm, which is the area between the shoulder and elbow. The pain can result from various causes such as muscle strain, overuse, injury, nerve irritation, or referred pain from the neck or shoulder. Patients typically experience discomfort, soreness, or aching in this specific arm location that may worsen with movement or certain activities.",
    "whoUses": "Primary care physicians, orthopedic specialists, physical medicine and rehabilitation doctors, and physical therapists commonly use this code when evaluating arm pain. It frequently appears on patient EOB statements for office visits, physical therapy, or imaging studies related to upper extremity complaints.",
